Package: watchmouse-host
Version: __VERSION__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-uinput, python3-cryptography
Maintainer: WinnyKing57 <winnyking57@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: WatchMouse Linux host (uinput)
 Turns the TCP input sent by a Wear OS watch into a real mouse and
 keyboard on a Linux desktop, using the uinput kernel module.
 The watch speaks a tiny newline-delimited JSON protocol over TCP
 (default port 8888); this package installs the receiver as a
 systemd service named watchmouse-host.
